WEBVTT

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:07.980
When it's a lucky day with nice weather

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:11.770
I hope we have a good time together

00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:15.620
Today let's keep

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:19.240
Sharing laughs

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:26.670
You take care of my true wishes in secret

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:34.220
You always cheer me up after bad days

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:40.580
I'm sure everyone has known it since childhood

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:49.250
You pretend you don't care, but you're always a good friend

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:58.650
You have another busy day as a god; you just can't help but help out others

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:04.990
Everyone is cheered up by your love

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:13.300
I love always being together while you help others

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:20.820
I'll protect that precious smile; you know what I mean

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:24.820
When it's a lucky day with nice weather

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:28.400
We should go visit the shrine together

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:44.150
Amane, the second wave of Nezumi seems very numerous!

00:01:44.150 --> 00:01:44.800
Yes!

00:01:49.190 --> 00:01:50.990
Please hold them off for a bit.

00:01:50.990 --> 00:01:52.430
Yes, Kukuri-sama!

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:04.470
I am your kingdom. Now, release them from suffering.

00:02:06.820 --> 00:02:09.280
Descend upon them, Heavenly Purging Flame!

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:26.000
It's over, Amane.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:27.940
Let's take a break.

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:29.270
Okay!

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.780
Kukuri-sama, we missed one!

00:02:33.550 --> 00:02:34.570
You're not getting away!

00:02:34.570 --> 00:02:35.340
Amane!

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:44.140
I did it.

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:49.410
Amane.

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:49.940
Yes?

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:55.870
That Nezumi had already abandoned its attempt to break into the vault. It was trying to escape.

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:58.700
You didn't need to kill it.

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:03.150
B-But, Kukuri-sama, they'll come back and attack the vault again if we let them go.

00:03:03.150 --> 00:03:05.840
And their numbers have grown somehow—

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:06.790
Amane!

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:11.070
Our responsibility is to guard the vault.

00:03:11.070 --> 00:03:14.020
It is <i>not to exterminate all the Nezumi.</i>

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:18.580
Now, Amane, I remember we have some hard candies.

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:20.090
Let's make tea, too.

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:24.560
But this way the fight won't ever end, will it?

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:29.020
Kukuri-sama, you'll be tied to this lunar shrine for eternity.

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:32.600
T-Tsukuyomi-sama!

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:38.820
My, that was an impressive fight, Kukuri-hime. You too, Amane-san.

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:41.100
You were watching us?

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:46.070
I was going to assist you if the situation became dangerous, but the two of you handled it just fine.

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:50.120
O-Oh, I'm flattered.

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:54.630
Still, they do seem more numerous, Kukuri-hime.

00:03:54.630 --> 00:03:56.700
Yes, somewhat.

00:03:56.700 --> 00:04:02.760
We have no choice. I wanted to give it more time, but we'll have to implement the plan now.

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:07.450
Oh, really? I was looking forward to it.

00:04:07.450 --> 00:04:08.570
"The plan"?

00:04:08.570 --> 00:04:14.550
Well, Amane, now that Tsukuyomi-sama is here, we'll take a break.

00:04:14.550 --> 00:04:16.200
Can you prepare some refreshments?

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:18.400
Oh, yes, right away.

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:30.200
What plan were they talking about?

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:41.260
Kukuri-sama seemed quite delighted as well.

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:50.220
Oh my, Tsukuyomi-sama, you haven't said anything to Mayu-san yet?

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:51.760
No.

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:53.390
I'm very sorry.

00:04:53.390 --> 00:04:56.650
I did tell my sister about it, though.

00:04:56.660 --> 00:05:01.740
Still, I'd really be glad if Mayu-san came here.

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:05.160
It's becoming difficult with just Amane and me.

00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:08.070
Amane-san is certainly competent,

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:12.080
but she's not good enough to be your successor, Kukuri-hime.

00:05:12.860 --> 00:05:15.330
When she has a junior to look after, I'm sure she'll—

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:17.950
Amane!

00:05:21.010 --> 00:05:23.340
Th-This is bad. She must've misunderstood something.

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:24.850
Please wait, Kukuri-hime.

00:05:25.910 --> 00:05:29.850
She wouldn't be able to handle the job for long,
if that was enough to upset her.

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:37.650
It's getting difficult with just Amane and me...

00:05:39.320 --> 00:05:41.970
...not good enough to be your successor, Kukuri-hime...

00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:46.890
So I'm not good enough!

00:05:46.890 --> 00:05:49.300
I'm not living up to their expectations!

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:52.870
I can't stay here anymore!

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:57.880
This place is different from that warm planet, after all.

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:06.800
Oh, an auspicious sign.

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:12.060
My, you believe in lucky omens as well? You're a goddess.

00:06:12.060 --> 00:06:14.630
I just have a feeling today.

00:06:14.630 --> 00:06:16.180
May I come in?

00:06:16.900 --> 00:06:19.310
I'm not banned from Heaven anymore?!

00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:25.320
Yes. Your mother, Akari-hime-sama, asked us to deliver a message along with this letter.

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:29.520
"Urgent matter. Return immediately," she says.

00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:31.490
She must be plotting something.

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:33.980
That's great to hear, Mayu!

00:06:33.980 --> 00:06:37.830
How about leaving Yuzu-san to me and
going back to Heaven right away?

00:06:38.740 --> 00:06:41.880
As if I'd leave Yuzu to a lousy guy like you!

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:46.390
Also, I like Yaoyorozu-dou a lot more than Heaven!

00:06:46.390 --> 00:06:48.260
My, Mayu-sama...

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:52.600
Compared to Heaven, the food here is better, and I can also play games as much as I want.

00:06:55.160 --> 00:06:58.480
A-Anyway, Sasana, relay this message to Mother.

00:06:58.480 --> 00:06:59.350
Sure.

00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:06.680
"I'm now an established deity here, with a shrine, albeit a small one. I'm no longer your puppet."

00:07:06.680 --> 00:07:07.440
That's small.

00:07:08.650 --> 00:07:11.380
Well, as I said, I'm not going back.

00:07:11.380 --> 00:07:13.840
I still have things I need to do.

00:07:13.840 --> 00:07:15.540
Things you need to do?

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:20.340
I have a major task: finishing the Kokumin Teki RPG.

00:07:22.070 --> 00:07:25.590
This BGM is just irresistible,

00:07:25.590 --> 00:07:27.460
so I'm going back to work.

00:07:28.780 --> 00:07:31.880
No, you don't, you lazy cat!

00:07:36.070 --> 00:07:37.890
Wh-Who are you?

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:47.630
There you go.

00:07:47.630 --> 00:07:48.650
Th-Thank you.

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:53.190
Then you're Kukuri-sama's guardian cat!

00:07:53.190 --> 00:07:55.160
I appreciate your hard work.

00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:59.670
Let me thank you on behalf of the Inari shrine as well.

00:07:59.670 --> 00:08:02.380
I don't deserve it. Lift your heads.

00:08:02.380 --> 00:08:05.230
Kukuri-sama is the amazing one, not me.

00:08:05.230 --> 00:08:12.680
And why is the <i>great guardian cat of the <i>great
Kukuri-sama sticking her nose into my lifestyle?</i></i>

00:08:13.890 --> 00:08:19.440
That's strange. Wasn't the tea stalk a sign of good luck?

00:08:13.890 --> 00:08:16.150
Jeez, Mayu-sama.

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:20.940
Um...

00:08:20.940 --> 00:08:23.690
Who is Kukuri-sama?

00:08:24.550 --> 00:08:26.560
Kukuri-sama guards a vault.

00:08:27.910 --> 00:08:35.270
She guards the lunar vault, a job given only to a cat god with outstanding valor and divine powers.

00:08:36.860 --> 00:08:43.410
Since ancient times, Amaterasu-sama
entrusted the cat gods to guard the vault.

00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:47.990
Earth's rats eat valuable harvests and precious scriptures,

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:54.210
but the Nezumi of the Underworld eat people's memories.

00:08:56.430 --> 00:08:58.430
Um, by "Underworld" you mean—

00:08:58.430 --> 00:09:00.810
The Underworld is the land of dead.

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:04.960
You just said that the the Nezumi eat memories.

00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:06.360
What does that mean?

00:09:06.360 --> 00:09:11.440
They eat the memories that people lose when they're asleep.

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:16.980
For example, memories of meals eaten three days ago or era names memorized in school.

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:20.080
What happens to people whose memories get eaten?

00:09:20.730 --> 00:09:24.500
It doesn't affect living people, so don't worry.

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:26.250
I see.

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:32.260
However, the lost memories stored in the lunar vault are always at risk.

00:09:32.830 --> 00:09:36.510
The Nezumi will devour all of them if we don't guard the vault.

00:09:38.260 --> 00:09:42.480
Well, they aren't powerful demons, but they're numerous.

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:45.660
Local cat gods deal with rats on Earth.

00:09:47.880 --> 00:09:52.630
We cat gods have the important duty
of guarding the vault from the Nezumi.

00:09:54.980 --> 00:10:00.090
That reminds me. The circular from the shopping district warned that there are more sewer rats lately.

00:10:00.090 --> 00:10:04.660
O-Ordinary cats are supposed to deal with sewer rats around here. It's not my responsibility!

00:10:04.660 --> 00:10:08.040
The local cat god is supposed to lead the local cats!

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:10.630
I'm trying in my own way!

00:10:10.630 --> 00:10:13.660
Why do I have to listen to your complaints?

00:10:13.660 --> 00:10:14.580
That's...

00:10:16.700 --> 00:10:21.800
That's because you're going to be
Kukuri-sama's guardian cat in my stead!

00:10:29.350 --> 00:10:32.320
W-Wait a second! I didn't hear about this!

00:10:33.330 --> 00:10:36.860
Mayu-sama, that's impressive! Amazing!

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:42.410
Oh, no, no, no, no way. There's no way Mayu could manage such an important job.

00:10:42.410 --> 00:10:45.450
Indeed, it must be a mistake.

00:10:45.450 --> 00:10:47.830
Just look. She's denying it herself.

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:53.040
There's no mistake, unless there's another cat god named Mayu.

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:56.150
Well, there isn't, but...

00:10:56.150 --> 00:10:57.630
You've sunk pretty low.

00:10:57.630 --> 00:10:58.330
Sunk? Come on.

00:10:58.980 --> 00:11:01.690
However, you're the only daughter of the leading cat god family.

00:11:01.690 --> 00:11:04.320
There's no problem with your lineage.

00:11:04.320 --> 00:11:07.560
You've earned Tsukuyomi-sama's favor. Be glad.

00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:10.350
Wh-What about my wishes?

00:11:10.350 --> 00:11:14.270
This is Tsukuyomi-sama's decision. Your wishes don't matter.

00:11:14.270 --> 00:11:15.980
That's unreasonable.

00:11:18.240 --> 00:11:20.910
Then what about you, Amane?

00:11:20.910 --> 00:11:24.370
Are you going to meekly accept the loss of your role as guardian cat?

00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:26.080
Th-That's...

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:28.250
Hey, Mayu, calm down.

00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:32.280
If it's their decision, I have to accept it.

00:11:35.970 --> 00:11:36.750
Follow me.

00:11:36.750 --> 00:11:37.550
Wh-What is it?

00:11:37.550 --> 00:11:38.760
Mayu-sama?

00:11:43.820 --> 00:11:47.150
This may be Tsukuyomi-sama's decision, but I don't understand it.

00:11:47.150 --> 00:11:49.590
We'll go to the Moon now and settle this face to face.

00:11:50.420 --> 00:11:52.650
Face to face? Are you serious?

00:11:52.650 --> 00:11:54.440
Of course I am!

00:11:54.440 --> 00:11:56.450
That's impossible!

00:11:56.450 --> 00:11:57.730
It isn't!

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:06.160
My goodness, Amane went to Mayu-san.

00:12:06.730 --> 00:12:09.660
Let's just watch them for now.

00:12:12.170 --> 00:12:13.670
All right.

00:12:14.640 --> 00:12:16.910
"Mayu-sama, it's sashimi for dinner!"

00:12:16.910 --> 00:12:18.670
Voiced by Mayu.

00:12:28.540 --> 00:12:34.490
In any case, our divine powers aren't sufficient
to transport us to the Moon.

00:12:34.490 --> 00:12:37.530
Th-That is... I guess you have a point.

00:12:38.220 --> 00:12:43.160
There's no choice, then. I don't want to,
but I'll have to return to Heaven this once.

00:12:43.160 --> 00:12:46.620
Then, Mayu-sama, tell your mother that—

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:51.500
No, I'm keeping this a secret from Mother. I'm not going back home.

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:54.380
My goal is just to visit Tsukuyomi-sama.

00:12:54.380 --> 00:12:58.100
Well, Mayu, feel free to take your time.

00:12:58.100 --> 00:13:01.560
Leave Yuzu-san to me while you're gone!

00:13:01.560 --> 00:13:04.890
As I've been saying, I won't leave her to you.

00:13:04.890 --> 00:13:07.460
Still, I'm reluctant to go.

00:13:07.460 --> 00:13:10.110
You don't want to go back to Heaven?

00:13:10.110 --> 00:13:12.630
Oh, of course not.

00:13:12.630 --> 00:13:16.410
Earth is more fun than a boring place like that.

00:13:16.410 --> 00:13:17.780
Don't you think so, Amane?

00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:26.670
Earth is fun? That never occurred to me.

00:13:44.310 --> 00:13:46.390
At least...

00:13:46.390 --> 00:13:49.560
I don't have good memories from Earth.

00:13:50.390 --> 00:13:51.630
Amane-san!

00:13:53.330 --> 00:13:54.700
Amane-san?

00:13:54.700 --> 00:13:55.570
Yes.

00:13:55.570 --> 00:13:57.570
Amane-san, would you like one?

00:13:59.570 --> 00:14:02.910
Jeez, Mayu, you're terrible at wrapping.

00:14:02.910 --> 00:14:04.580
Am I?

00:14:04.580 --> 00:14:06.580
Gonta, your way is too complex.

00:14:06.580 --> 00:14:08.590
You're being too sloppy!

00:14:08.590 --> 00:14:11.330
I'll do it for you, Mayu-sama.

00:14:12.270 --> 00:14:14.080
Sasana, don't spoil her!

00:14:15.090 --> 00:14:17.130
Amane, have one before leaving!

00:14:17.130 --> 00:14:18.720
But...

00:14:18.720 --> 00:14:20.090
It's all right.

00:14:20.090 --> 00:14:23.890
Amane-san, you'll stay here for the night, right?

00:14:23.890 --> 00:14:27.430
N-No, I can't inconvenience you like that.

00:14:27.430 --> 00:14:28.850
Just stay here overnight.

00:14:28.850 --> 00:14:30.350
Please do.

00:14:32.160 --> 00:14:33.360
Sure.

00:14:33.360 --> 00:14:36.860
It would bother me if you left now, you know.

00:14:48.370 --> 00:14:51.420
For this occasion, um...

00:14:51.420 --> 00:14:54.290
we are absolutely humbled by the delightful news.

00:14:54.290 --> 00:14:56.550
Please lift your heads.

00:14:58.070 --> 00:15:01.380
What did Mayu do now?

00:15:01.380 --> 00:15:05.470
How did things turn out this way?

00:15:05.470 --> 00:15:08.220
Please. Raise your heads.

00:15:08.220 --> 00:15:08.970
Yes!

00:15:08.970 --> 00:15:16.360
My little brother insists on Mayu-san,
so I'd like you two to understand.

00:15:16.360 --> 00:15:18.780
W-We are humbled.

00:15:18.780 --> 00:15:23.860
Still, what did a great god like Tsukuyomi-sama ever see in Mayu?

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:29.170
Oh my, Mayu-san is said to be quite witty and clever.

00:15:32.880 --> 00:15:35.450
Then, I'm counting on you.

00:15:35.450 --> 00:15:36.520
Right!

00:15:37.760 --> 00:15:41.930
Why hasn't Mayu come back? I told her it was urgent!

00:15:41.930 --> 00:15:46.160
Calm down. You don't have to get angry.

00:15:46.160 --> 00:15:48.450
I can't help getting angry!

00:15:48.450 --> 00:15:51.510
Goodness, why couldn't she just come back?

00:15:54.770 --> 00:15:57.190
My, it's chestnut rice tonight!

00:15:59.190 --> 00:16:01.940
I hope you like it, Amane-san.

00:16:01.940 --> 00:16:03.700
It looks delicious!

00:16:03.700 --> 00:16:06.000
Please don't hold back.

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:07.240
Okay.

00:16:07.240 --> 00:16:11.150
I'm happy just to enjoy your home cooking, Yuzu-san.

00:16:12.630 --> 00:16:17.670
Please don't hold back. Take as much as you want, Gonta-san!

00:16:17.670 --> 00:16:18.880
Y-Yuzu-san!

00:16:19.700 --> 00:16:20.880
You fell for it.

00:16:20.880 --> 00:16:22.510
Meiko, when did you get here?

00:16:22.510 --> 00:16:26.260
Did you pick up the chestnut rice aroma, Meiko?

00:16:26.260 --> 00:16:30.770
Don't treat me like I'm a pig snuffling for truffles!

00:16:30.770 --> 00:16:34.890
I didn't mean that, but I guess you know yourself best.

00:16:34.890 --> 00:16:41.550
I thought a feast this enjoyable wouldn't
take off without me, so I came over.

00:16:41.550 --> 00:16:46.380
I tagged along, too. It's always great to eat together!

00:16:46.380 --> 00:16:51.290
Unlike a certain someone, I brought a courtesy gift as well!

00:16:53.800 --> 00:16:56.540
Meiko's planning to lure Mayu-sama with treats!

00:16:56.540 --> 00:16:59.540
Oh, more chestnut treats!

00:16:59.540 --> 00:17:02.640
I heard these cakes are really good!

00:17:02.640 --> 00:17:04.310
Here!

00:17:04.310 --> 00:17:06.630
Try one, Mayu!

00:17:06.630 --> 00:17:10.430
Oh, it's a chestnut festival tonight!

00:17:11.530 --> 00:17:14.060
It's lively today. I love it!

00:17:14.060 --> 00:17:16.140
Everyone, let's dig in.

00:17:16.140 --> 00:17:19.040
Gonta, you're taking too many chestnuts from the chestnut rice!

00:17:19.040 --> 00:17:20.570
You're not the one to talk, Meiko!

00:17:20.570 --> 00:17:22.010
Don't fight!

00:17:22.010 --> 00:17:23.460
There's a lot!

00:17:23.460 --> 00:17:24.790
Don't be so stingy!

00:17:24.790 --> 00:17:26.570
You took the biggest chestnut, Mayu!

00:17:26.570 --> 00:17:27.990
Don't be so stingy!

00:17:27.990 --> 00:17:29.130
There's enough for everyone.

00:17:29.130 --> 00:17:30.570
Don't be so stingy!

00:17:33.790 --> 00:17:38.520
I was only going to see Mayu for a minute. How did this happen?

00:17:39.510 --> 00:17:44.990
No, I wasn't. I didn't have any place else to go, after all.

00:17:44.990 --> 00:17:48.340
Yes. I don't belong anywhere now.

00:17:53.750 --> 00:17:57.440
I guess I'll repay part of the favor by keeping watch tonight.

00:17:58.480 --> 00:18:00.350
Is that a Nezumi?

00:18:00.350 --> 00:18:01.900
You aren't getting away!

00:18:02.860 --> 00:18:04.650
You need to settle down, Amane.

00:18:06.180 --> 00:18:08.360
It's just a sewer rat.

00:18:08.360 --> 00:18:10.410
It didn't do anything bad.

00:18:10.410 --> 00:18:12.610
There's no need to kill it, is there?

00:18:12.900 --> 00:18:19.110
That Nezumi had already abandoned its attempt to break into the vault and was trying to escape.

00:18:19.110 --> 00:18:21.870
You didn't need to kill it.

00:18:26.010 --> 00:18:27.380
What's wrong?

00:18:27.380 --> 00:18:29.710
Weren't you asleep?

00:18:29.710 --> 00:18:32.870
Your bloodthirsty emotions woke me up.

00:18:32.870 --> 00:18:36.140
M-My bad. I forgot I'm on Earth.

00:18:36.140 --> 00:18:39.920
The number of Nezumi in the lunar shrine
has been unusually high lately.

00:18:39.920 --> 00:18:41.680
I probably got too anxious.

00:18:41.680 --> 00:18:43.680
An unusual proliferation of Nezumi?

00:18:43.680 --> 00:18:45.220
Yes.

00:18:46.430 --> 00:18:48.650
Anyway, I apologize.

00:18:50.550 --> 00:18:51.860
Mind coming with me for a bit?

00:18:58.310 --> 00:19:00.270
Master, this tastes great!

00:19:00.270 --> 00:19:02.370
Thank you very much.

00:19:02.570 --> 00:19:04.800
How is it? Isn't it good?

00:19:04.800 --> 00:19:05.830
Uh-huh.

00:19:05.830 --> 00:19:10.100
Yuzu's cooking is great, but something like this is nice once in a while.

00:19:12.540 --> 00:19:14.160
So let's keep talking.

00:19:14.920 --> 00:19:17.500
About the unusual proliferation of Nezumi, I mean.

00:19:18.300 --> 00:19:22.500
Kukuri-sama and I might not be able to guard the lunar vault by ourselves.

00:19:22.500 --> 00:19:26.410
That's probably why Tsukuyomi-sama selected you.

00:19:27.410 --> 00:19:31.230
I can't believe Tsukuyomi-sama chose me. He must be weird.

00:19:31.230 --> 00:19:34.600
Yeah, no kidding! I was born an ordinary cat.

00:19:34.600 --> 00:19:39.240
I worked desperately to become a guardian cat.

00:19:39.240 --> 00:19:42.740
I don't have a clue! I'm the one who'd like to ask.

00:19:42.740 --> 00:19:44.490
Eat. The noodles will get soggy.

00:19:44.490 --> 00:19:47.130
I worked so hard.

00:19:47.130 --> 00:19:50.240
Why was a lazy cat like you named to replace me?

00:19:50.240 --> 00:19:52.000
As I said, eat before the noodles get soggy.

00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:54.220
You're naive, little lady.

00:19:54.220 --> 00:19:56.250
Your arrogance is to blame.

00:19:56.250 --> 00:19:58.260
Huh? What do you mean?

00:19:58.260 --> 00:20:00.930
Ah, you had to ask.

00:20:00.930 --> 00:20:03.510
I see. You want me to tell you.

00:20:03.510 --> 00:20:05.760
He'll be talking for a while.

00:20:05.760 --> 00:20:13.900
Because of my arrogance, I'm running a small ramen cart now.

00:20:13.900 --> 00:20:15.620
He's started.

00:20:15.620 --> 00:20:18.890
Hey, Amane, you don't need to listen. Just hurry up and eat.

00:20:18.890 --> 00:20:19.820
O-Okay.

00:20:19.820 --> 00:20:23.280
After falling to the very bottom, I've worked my way up from square one.

00:20:23.280 --> 00:20:30.290
When I could just about manage a decent living, I met the "nan pla of life."

00:20:30.290 --> 00:20:33.190
That nan pla ramen was a big hit.

00:20:33.190 --> 00:20:36.710
I raced up the stairway of fortune after that.

00:20:39.380 --> 00:20:44.800
When we have a major stroke of luck,
we tend to lose sight of ordinary happiness.

00:20:44.800 --> 00:20:50.680
I got too full of myself, focused on making money, and lost everything.

00:20:50.680 --> 00:20:54.350
Jeez, I might even be possessed by the Goddess of Poverty.

00:20:54.350 --> 00:20:56.560
One nan pla ramen.

00:20:56.550 --> 00:20:58.660
Oh, Shamo-san.

00:20:58.660 --> 00:21:01.570
You're the Ame-no-Sagiri goddess, Shamo-sama!

00:21:01.570 --> 00:21:08.800
Until recently, the nan pla ramen had way too much nan pla in it, which made it too fishy to eat.

00:21:08.800 --> 00:21:12.020
But I think they've finally figured out the right balance.

00:21:12.020 --> 00:21:13.500
You're quite the gourmet.

00:21:13.500 --> 00:21:15.870
You're not the only one at fault, President!

00:21:15.870 --> 00:21:19.130
As I keep saying, I no longer hold that title.

00:21:19.130 --> 00:21:21.580
One nan pla ramen.

00:21:21.580 --> 00:21:25.630
Firm noodles, a little more nan pla, and extra pork.

00:21:25.630 --> 00:21:29.570
President, if one god deserts you, another will recycle you!

00:21:29.570 --> 00:21:31.390
You're right!

00:21:31.390 --> 00:21:35.130
Master, there's a customer requesting ramen.

00:21:35.130 --> 00:21:38.670
Firm noodles, a little more nan pla, and extra pork.

00:21:38.670 --> 00:21:39.400
Coming right up!

00:21:39.400 --> 00:21:41.390
Mayu, thank you as always.

00:21:39.400 --> 00:21:44.090
Firm noodles, a little more nan pla, and extra pork... huh?

00:21:41.390 --> 00:21:42.400
No problem.

00:22:02.140 --> 00:22:09.190
I gently peered into the future which we call tomorrow

00:22:09.190 --> 00:22:13.320
Looking at the world upside down

00:22:13.360 --> 00:22:20.360
I projected my memories upon the glittering cotton candy clouds

00:22:20.360 --> 00:22:24.490
And hung rainbow ribbons

00:22:24.490 --> 00:22:31.790
When I'm left alone, I feel lonely and depressed

00:22:32.210 --> 00:22:38.260
So stay here forever

00:22:38.260 --> 00:22:43.510
I'm sure everyone has some

00:22:43.510 --> 00:22:49.430
Unfulfilled desires locked inside their hearts

00:22:51.690 --> 00:23:01.610
I want you to realize that small memory that won't disappear is the key. Yeah

00:23:01.610 --> 00:23:08.080
You're always the only one

00:23:08.080 --> 00:23:12.370
Who can make me reminisce fondly

00:23:26.400 --> 00:23:41.370
Next Episode

00:23:27.180 --> 00:23:29.700
Yuzu, this is going to be a pain to deal with.

00:23:29.700 --> 00:23:32.090
Mayu-sama, are you going back to Heaven?

00:23:32.090 --> 00:23:33.410
Well, I'll drop by and—

00:23:33.410 --> 00:23:36.750
Sasana, Meiko! You know something, don't you?

00:23:36.750 --> 00:23:38.340
Know what?

00:23:38.340 --> 00:23:39.230
I don't know!

00:23:38.410 --> 00:23:41.370
Stray Cats Run After

00:23:39.230 --> 00:23:41.300
No, no!
